{"step_index":385,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:33:53Z","thinking":"**Standardizing Script Paths**\n\nThe goal is to ensure the script's `ANSIBLE_DIR` is correctly and consistently determined regardless of how it's invoked. Employing a method that resolves symlinks, specifically using a tool that finds the absolute path of the script, will help. This avoids ambiguity whether the script is run directly or through a symbolic link. Implementing this strategy ensures that the `ANSIBLE_DIR` always points to the intended location.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/search-servers.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ==============================================================================\n# Script: search-servers.sh\n# Purpose: Instant CLI search across the KeePass server pool.\n#          Can also trigger a full sync if the database changed.\n# ==============================================================================\n\nset -eo pipefail\n\nREAL_PATH=\"$(readlink -f \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\"\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${REAL_PATH}\")\" && pwd)\"\nANSIBLE_DIR=\"$(cd \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/..\" && pwd)\"\nPOOL_JSON=\"${ANSIBLE_DIR}/inventory/server_pool.json\"\nPARSER=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/build_kdbx_pool.py\"\n\nC_RESET=$'\\033[0m'\nC_BOLD=$'\\033[1m'\nC_GREEN=$'\\033[0;32m'\nC_YELLOW=$'\\033[0;33m'\nC_BLUE=$'\\033[0;34m'\n\nusage() {\n    cat << USAGE\n${C_BOLD}Usage:${C_RESET}\n    $(basename \"$0\") <SEARCH_TERM>\n    $(basename \"$0\") --sync [--db <PATH_TO_KDBX>]\n\n${C_BOLD}Description:${C_RESET}\n    Searches your KeePass server pool across Hostnames, IPs, Usernames,\n    Groups, and Notes in milliseconds.\n\n${C_BOLD}Options:${C_RESET}\n    --sync                 Prompt for master password and rebuild the server pool\n    --db <PATH>            Specify alternative .kdbx path (default: Documents/keePassXC/OMT_PFS.SYSTEME.ALL.kdbx)\n    -j, --json             Output raw JSON for scripting/automation\n    -h, --help             Show this help message\n\n${C_BOLD}Examples:${C_RESET}\n    $(basename \"$0\") 172.30.231\n    $(basename \"$0\") mail\n    $(basename \"$0\") superuser\n    $(basename \"$0\") --sync\nUSAGE\n    exit 0\n}\n\nif [[ $# -eq 0 ]]; then\n    usage\nfi\n\nSYNC=false\nJSON_OUT=false\nDB_PATH=\"\"\nSEARCH_TERM=\"\"\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n    case \"$1\" in\n        -h|--help)\n            usage\n            ;;\n        --sync)\n            SYNC=true\n            shift\n            ;;\n        --db)\n            DB_PATH=\"$2\"\n            shift 2\n            ;;\n        -j|--json)\n            JSON_OUT=true\n            shift\n            ;;\n        *)\n            SEARCH_TERM=\"$1\"\n            shift\n            ;;\n    esac\ndone\n\nif [ \"$SYNC\" = true ] || [ ! -f \"$POOL_JSON\" ]; then\n    echo -e \"${C_BOLD}=== [Synchronizing Server Pool from KeePass] ===${C_RESET}\"\n    read -s -p \"Enter KeePass Master Password: \" MASTER_PASS\n    echo \"\"\n    \n    EXTRA_ARGS=()\n    if [ -n \"$DB_PATH\" ]; then\n        EXTRA_ARGS+=(\"--db\" \"$DB_PATH\")\n    fi\n    if [ -n \"$SEARCH_TERM\" ]; then\n        EXTRA_ARGS+=(\"--search\" \"$SEARCH_TERM\")\n    fi\n    if [ \"$JSON_OUT\" = true ]; then\n        EXTRA_ARGS+=(\"--json-output\")\n    fi\n\n    echo \"$MASTER_PASS\" | \"$PARSER\" \"${EXTRA_ARGS[@]}\" --sync\n    unset MASTER_PASS\n    exit 0\nfi\n\n# Fast search using cached pool\nCMD=(\"$PARSER\" \"--search\" \"$SEARCH_TERM\")\nif [ \"$JSON_OUT\" = true ]; then\n    CMD+=(\"--json-output\")\nfi\n\n\"${CMD[@]}\"\nEOF\nchmod +x /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/search-servers.sh\n","Cwd":"/home/koby/.ansible","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Fix path resolution in search-servers.sh"}}]}
