{"step_index":399,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:35:48Z","content":"Sharp eye! Here is exactly why that happened and how I just patched it:\n\n### Why It Appeared\n\n1. **Not the KeePass `Password` Field**: The parser never exported the primary encrypted `Password` field for `superuser`.\n2. **Leaked via Free-Text `Notes`**: Inside KeePass, someone jotted down secondary root credentials directly into the entry's free-text **Notes** field (`root / cy/...`). Because the initial version of the search engine displayed the `Notes` field verbatim, that text leaked onto the screen.\n\n---\n\n### What I Patched & Secured\n\n#### 1. Automatic Password Masking\nUpdated [scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py](file:///home/koby/.ansible/scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py) with an active credential sanitizer:\n- Detects credential patterns in notes such as `<user> / <secret>`, `password: <secret>`, `mdp: <secret>`, and `root: <secret>`.\n- Automatically replaces sensitive strings with **`[PROTECTED]`**.\n- Immediately scrubbed your local [inventory/server_pool.json](file:///home/koby/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json) and [inventory/server_pool.yml](file:///home/koby/.inventory/server_pool.yml) on disk so no plain passwords linger.\n\n#### 2. Enhanced Port Detection (`ssh30://`)\nKeePass URLs using the internal `ssh30://172.30.39.153` scheme are now automatically parsed to extract **`Port: 30`**.\n\n---\n\n### Verification: Running the Search Again\n\nNow when you search for `mtq-mailsrvp-01`:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.ansible\nansible-playbook playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml -e \"search=mtq-mailsrvp-01\"\n```\n\n**Clean Output**:\n```text\n=== [Search Results for 'mtq-mailsrvp-01': 1 match(es)] ===\n\n   1. mtq-mailsrvp-01 [SSH]\n      IP(s)   : 172.30.39.153 Port: 30\n      User    : superuser\n      Group   : OMT_PFS.SYSTEME.ALL/MTQ/linux\n      Notes   : root / [PROTECTED]\n```\n\n*(Or via the instant CLI helper: `./search-servers.sh mtq-mailsrvp-01`)*.\n\n---\n\n### Need to View Secrets on Demand?\n\nIf you ever intentionally want to reveal the protected password string for an entry:\n\n- **Via Ansible Playbook**:\n  ```bash\n  ansible-playbook playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml -e \"search=mtq-mailsrvp-01\" -e \"reveal=true\"\n  ```\n- **Via CLI Script**:\n  ```bash\n  ./search-servers.sh -r mtq-mailsrvp-01\n  ```\n\nBy default, all sensitive credential patterns remain masked as <span style=\"color:yellow\">`[PROTECTED]`</span> across both the terminal and your Ansible inventory files.","thinking":"**Tracing Note Retrieval Source**\n\nThe system replaces raw notes within the configuration.  A `--reveal` flag reveals these notes. The unmasked information originates either from synchronizing and storing the raw notes, or from a database query. The KeePass password attribute was never exported.\n\n\n"}
